Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "3. Results: Predictions for the number of double degenerate mergers \
exceeding 1.0",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["M", "\[Sun]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "429713bc-1952-4cce-8480-f1af54235411"],
 " in the 100 pc sample"
}], "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965185955111462*^9, 3.96518600812856*^9}, {
   3.993766547101716*^9, 3.99376655911677*^9}, {3.993766669039077*^9, 
   3.993766705677569*^9}, 
   3.993775430424816*^9},ExpressionUUID->"9e2131b9-8287-4c3a-973f-\
4d9cb8f61040"],

Cell["\<\
This calculation is a prediction for the number distribution of short period \
CO+CO binaries with merger timescales << Hubble time (i.e. < Gyr or so, \
orbital period < few hours.)

The number distribution relies on a constant merger rate, so is only \
applicable if the population is heading towards merger in < Gyr. In other \
words, for a population of binaries heading toward gravitational wave driven \
merger, the production rate = destruction rate (constant star formation rate) \
= \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]steady state\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. This \
assumption is valid in the Milky Way over Myr timescales, but not over Gyr \
e.g. https://noirlab.edu/public/images/noao1903c/

This technique was first developed for binary black hole mergers (Kyutoku and \
Seto 2016) and later binary neutron stars (McNeill and Seto 2022). But it has \
more recently been applied to double white dwarfs (Seto 2023, McNeill and \
Hirai 2025)

Finally we compare this to the observed population of CO + CO binaries in \
this special short-period regime.
Currently there is ONE!\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.993766125736774*^9, 3.993766319540065*^9}, 
   3.9937665250312643`*^9, {3.993766831186626*^9, 3.993766938223921*^9}, {
   3.993767001347204*^9, 3.993767076484117*^9}, {3.99376714332688*^9, 
   3.993767159273014*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8f0a1aaf-651f-4a46-84b0-\
d1fc59115def"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Chirp mass distribution from 1b.", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9937669662462473`*^9, 3.993766976941557*^9}, {
   3.993767801013804*^9, 3.993767811203569*^9}, 
   3.993770340596986*^9},ExpressionUUID->"f5cb05d0-8954-4310-97b5-\
3857795fca9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Mchirpf", "[", 
    RowBox[{"m11_", ",", "m22_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"m11", " ", "m22"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"3", "/", "5"}]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"m11", "+", "m22"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "5"}]]]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:=",ExpressionUUID->"dfbfcc25-8deb-490f-badc-f705d1bf704c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

